# Version Bump Before Push

Before every `git push`, bump the patch version in `package.json`:

```bash
npm version patch --no-git-tag-version
```

This updates the version (e.g., `0.0.2` → `0.0.3`) which gets embedded in the HTML during build for deployment verification.

## Workflow

1. Make your changes
2. Run `npm version patch --no-git-tag-version`
3. Commit all changes (including package.json version bump)
4. Push to remote

## Verification

After deployment, check the site's HTML for the version:
- DevTools → Elements → `<body data-version="X.X.X">`
- View Source → Look for `<!-- Build: vX.X.X | timestamp -->`
